the tablet holds a subset of the library as plain files, copied one way from
the laptop, and serves them to its own chrome. the laptop is the truth; the
tablet is a clone of the part named in `medium/path/keep`, one path per
line from the library's root.

three scripts do it, and the page is unchanged. `medium/path/pull` copies
what keep names from the laptop with rsync. `medium/path/serve` serves the
copy at localhost:8080 with quark.mjs under node. `medium/path/bootstrap`
sets up a fresh tablet.

termux runs them: a linux userland as an android app. pkg installs rsync,
openssh and node; sshd on port 8022 lets the laptop log in and drive the
tablet. each side's key is in the other's authorized_keys, so pull and ssh
ask for nothing. a new tablet starts with one command in termux:

  pkg install -y openssh \
  && scp tnishant@192.168.29.13:src/sys/medium/path/bootstrap . \
  && sh bootstrap

bootstrap ends by printing the step no script can take: grant all-files
access, force stop termux, reopen it.

the tablet keeps its own copy of keep and edits it there. the one in this
folder is the list the tablet was set up with; copy the tablet's back after
editing, or a lost tablet takes its list with it.

finding the tablet: the router hands out its address, 192.168.29.27 when
this was written. if it moves, a scan for sshd finds it:

  for i in $(seq 254); do
    (timeout .5 bash -c "echo >/dev/tcp/192.168.29.$i/8022" 2>/dev/null \
    && echo 192.168.29.$i) &
  done; wait

the tablet's address matters only for driving it from the laptop. pull
needs the laptop's, 192.168.29.13; that is the one to reserve in the router.

rejected
  a service worker caching the subset inside chrome, with no termux:
    about 60 lines of new code, a developer flag (plain http is not a
    secure context), copies no other app can open, and eviction under
    storage pressure. here the copies are files
  syncthing: two-way sync, a daemon, a protocol. the need is one way
  quark itself: it chroots, and android refuses that without root. serve
    runs quark.mjs, which pull brings along with the library

surprises
  shared storage refuses chmod and utime, so rsync -a fails there
  all-files access reaches only a new termux process: grant, force stop,
    reopen, sshd. until then termux can still write documents/ and
    download/, which hides the missing grant
  pkill -f quark.mjs over ssh matches its own command line and kills the
    session
  chrome on android has no pdf viewer: a pdf in a frame is downloaded and
    opened in drive. the page draws it with pdf.js instead, fetched once
    from cdnjs and cached a year, so it works offline after one online open

deferred
  ticks and places live per origin: localhost:8080 on the tablet and
    192.168.29.13:8080 on the laptop keep separate sets
  pull never deletes: a path dropped from keep stays on the tablet
  pull skips a file whose size matches, so an edit that keeps the size
    is not copied
  a new subject's path.md is not in keep until added by hand
  serve does not start on its own; termux:boot would
  nothing notices that the laptop came up; pull runs by hand
  pdf.js draws no text layer: a pdf's text cannot be selected or found,
    and no place in it is kept

check: on the tablet, wifi off, reload localhost:8080/path.html. the
outline and every kept file open; the rest is struck through.
